{"Title":"Order relative to authorizing the joint committee on Transportation to make an investigation and study of certain current Senate documents transportation planning and revenue,","BillNumber":"S2796","DocketNumber":null,"GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"J27","Name":"Joint Committee on Transportation","Type":2,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J27","ResponseDate":"2024-05-23T08:48:58.22"},"Cosponsors":[],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2796/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Order","Pinslip":"May, 23, 2024 -- The committee on Transportation, to whom was referred the petitions (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 566) of Pavel M. Payano and Steven Owens for legislation to support better commuting; (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 2227) of Julian Cyr, Joanne M. Comerford, Jack Patrick Lewis, Sean Garballey and other members of the General Court for legislation to end debt-based driving restrictions and remove economic roadblocks; (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 2231) of Lydia Edwards, Michael D. Brady, Sal N. DiDomenico, Vanna Howard and other members of the General Court for legislation to establish a program for low income fares (LIF); and (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 2261) of Joan B. Lovely for legislation relative to online driver education, report the accompanying Order  (Senate, No. 2796).","DocumentText":"\tOrdered, That the committee on Transportation be authorized and directed to make an investigation and study of certain current Senate documents numbered 566, 2227, 2231, and 2261 relative to transportation planning and revenue.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Study","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J27","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J27"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Discharge to Another Committee","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J40","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J40"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}